---
description: Add a package as a direct dependency instead of inlining its types, enums, or string values.
globs: '**/*.{ts,tsx},package.json'
alwaysApply: false
---

# Add a direct dependency instead of inlining its API

If you need a type, enum, or function from a package, import it and list that
package in `package.json`. Do not copy its string values or types into our
code to avoid an import.

`import/no-extraneous-dependencies` means the package is missing from
`package.json` (often it is only a transitive dependency). Fix that with
`yarn add <package>`. Do not work around the lint by inlining the API.

```ts
// Bad — copied react-dropzone strings to avoid importing the package
switch (error.code) {
  case 'file-invalid-type':
    return `${file.name} is not a PDF.`;
}

// Good — direct dependency + library enum
import { ErrorCode } from 'react-dropzone';

switch (error.code) {
  case ErrorCode.FileInvalidType:
    return `${file.name} is not a PDF.`;
}
```
